- op: create  # 34ef
  at: '2026-04-07T01:59:38Z'  # 34ef
  by: agent  # 34ef
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 34ef
  clock: 1  # 34ef
  nonce: 34ef  # 34ef
  data:  # 34ef
    kind: invariant  # 34ef
    title: "library_patterns YAML never applied to edges (scan_library_patterns is dead code)"  # 34ef
    status: violated  # 34ef
    priority: 0  # 34ef
    parent:  # 34ef
    tags:  # 34ef
    - analysis_quality  # 34ef
    - cross_language_linkers  # 34ef
    before: []  # 34ef
    duplicate_of: []  # 34ef
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 34ef
    pr_ref:  # 34ef
    description: "Highest-impact remaining bakeoff finding from deep-20260406-161630 and deep-20260406-182616. Verified by reading dataflow.py source: scan_library_patterns is defined and unit-tested but never integrated. Fix: add a library-patterns annotation pass to annotate_dataflow (or call scan_library_patterns from each analyzer's _annotate_dataflow integration point) that maps DataflowSite line numbers back to call edges and stamps access_mode into edge.meta. Likely affects all 5 languages with library_patterns: Go (30 patterns), Python, Rust, TS, Java. Bakeoff impact: prometheus LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO 5.1% → expected to clear; alertmanager dimension_scores.dataflow_annotation_quality 2 → expected ≥4."  # 34ef
    fields:  # 34ef
      statement: "Every YAML library_patterns entry (e.g. Go's '\\.Set\\(' → write, Python's '\\.append\\(' → write) must be matched against source files and the resulting access_mode must propagate to call edges so that --dataflow slices have something to filter on."  # 34ef
      root_cause: "dataflow.py defines scan_library_patterns(content, config) which produces DataflowSite objects from regex matches, but the function is only called from test_dataflow.py — no analyzer (Go, Python, Rust, TS, Java, etc.) integrates it into the edge annotation pipeline. The analyzers call annotate_dataflow(edges, tree, source, config) which only applies the AST positional rules from the assignments/returns sections; library_patterns is silently dropped. Result: in alertmanager hg.json, of 8872 calls edges, 4520 have access_mode='read' (from a different code path) but ZERO have 'write' or 'mutate' despite 15 Go write patterns existing in go.yaml. The dataflow slice consequently has 0 access-mode-annotated edges, manifesting as the LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO bakeoff WARN on prometheus."  # 34ef
