- op: discuss  # b3e4
  at: '2026-04-07T07:37:51Z'  # b3e4
  by: agent  # b3e4
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b3e4
  clock: 9  # b3e4
  nonce: b3e4  # b3e4
  message: "Both wiring fixes confirmed by deep-20260407-030917 reflect agents. (1) PR #2733 (commit a3ec56fed) wired scan_library_patterns into annotate_dataflow (tree-sitter pipeline used by 10 analyzers including go.py); alertmanager Go edges with access_mode=write went from 0 to 274. (2) PR #2740 (commit b5680c151) extended this to annotate_dataflow_ast (the stdlib ast variant used by py.py); kserve Python edges now carry library_pattern access_modes for 359/361 method calls (99.4% coverage). The original concrete impact estimate (98 .append + 37 .update + 30 .write = 0 access_mode) is now (98 .append + 37 .update + 30 .write = correctly tagged). Prometheus LOW_DATAFLOW_SLICE_RATIO WARN persists at 6.0% but this is now a denominator effect from forward slice growing faster than dataflow annotations, not the dead-code bug INV-halar described."  # b3e4
